---
import Legal from "../components/Legal.astro";
import { site, instagramUrl } from "../config";
---

<Legal title="Privacy policy" updated="15 September 2026">
  <p>
    This site and its Instagram automation are run by @{site.handle}, one person. This page covers
    what gets collected when you visit this site or comment on one of my reels, and nothing is
    sold or shared for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, no sign-up, no cookies.</li>
    <li>
      Visits are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless and doesn't track you
      across sites. It records aggregate things like page views, referrer, country and device type.
    </li>
    <li>When you tap a tool, a click counter for that tool goes up by one. It doesn't record who you are.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Comments and direct messages on Instagram</h2>
  <p>
    If you comment the keyword on one of my reels, an automated system replies to you by direct
    message with the link you asked for. To do that it uses Instagram's official API and handles:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the ID of your comment and your Instagram-scoped user ID, so it replies once and not twice;</li>
    <li>whether you follow my account, checked only after you message back, to decide whether to send the link;</li>
    <li>the messages in that one conversation, only to notice that you replied.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Those IDs are stored for at most 14 days and then deleted. Message contents aren't stored.
    Nothing is used for anything other than sending you the link.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>See <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion</a>.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Message <a href={instagramUrl} rel="noopener">@{site.handle}</a> on Instagram.</p>
</Legal>
